OrionLayer open fix 114 — the map's two event banners on the wire
==================================================================

Work order 403 (package B). orion2re on the fork's branch `orionlayer`
(v2.0.0), on top of open fix 115 and its README row. Not on
`orionlayer-local`. In src/ext/ext_api.cpp only, under ORION2RE_EXT (the
file is compiled only with it).

The main screen prints two banners while an event runs
(mainscr_main.cpp:28-43, the word ESTR_BEAST at the top left with two
lines above and below; :45-59, the hyperspace flux's H 0xE0 message at the
right). Their conditions are EVENTS::Event_Check_Warp_Beast
(events.cpp:217-225: event_data[EVENT_WARP_BEAST].status is 2, 4 or 6, for
every player) and Event_Check_Hyperspace_Flux (events.cpp:207-215). event_data
is in no block of the snapshot, so a client could not know.

The change. SerializeState writes "EVTB" on every screen, before FILM (FILM
stays the last block): uint8 version (1), uint8 the warp beast's event is
active, uint8 the hyperspace flux's event is. Both functions only read
event_data. Seven bytes per snapshot.

Live: UNVERIFIED — no live run (Data's decision of 20 October 2026; work
order 403 does not run the engine). Built on the scratch clone
`~/claude/clones/403_orion2re` (`linux-debug`, ORION2RE_EXT on); a misspelt
call (`Event_Check_Warp_BeastX`) is refused by the compiler.

